{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141300-my-homebrew-setting-for-dream-stuff","id":1141300,"title":"My homebrew setting for Dream Stuff.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-17T20:59:01-07:00","id":1141300,"title":"My homebrew setting for Dream Stuff.","content":"In my game Dreamstuff isn't exactly rare, but due to the variety, and the fact that harvesting it from the Dreaming can literally cost you an arm and a leg, I decided that the Sidhe through the Crystal Circle offer mundane wealth as well as offer to use of their power over the Arts in exchange for Dreamstuff, particularly certain types. Some of the more adventurous and skilled Changelings (and even some Chimera) make a full time living off of this. <br /> <br /> Some of the more authoritarian realms even demand that all Dreamstuff be turned over to the local lord for safekeeping until it is authorized to be used by licensed relic smiths. There is a big underground black market in some places for Dreamstuff and various guilds grumble over the royal licenses that are demanded to work with the 'Stuff on the grounds that such precious resources mustn't be risked being wasted by an inept crafter. Others note that this has been an excellent way for the Sidhe to keep a monopoly on all but a few of the most powerful Treasures produced. <br /> <br /> So, thoughts?<br /> <br /> Edit: And in the Dreaming there are small villages of Changelings and/or Chimera that specialize in gathering Dreamstuff, not unlike small outposts that used to specialize in gathering and trading furs. They trade with visitors from the mundane realm in exchange for finished Treasures that have been properly Sained, knowledge of Arts and Realms, or even different types of Dreamstuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-18-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T05:02:41-07:00","id":1141374,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a very good setting to be honest. But if you have a economy over dreamstuff it is necessary a demand for it too. Those outposts probably have deals with market freeholds nearby to commercialize this stuff. Even far away Market Freeholds might be interested, so caravans might be taking those goods from one place to another, maybe across countries.<br /> <br /> Also outposts might go after different stuff than just furs, like minerals (Gold, silver, esmeraldas, iron), wood and herbs, hunting and capturing different kinds of Animal Chimera (horses, dogs, wolfs, lions, gryphons, etc.). Also Also, remember that staying in the Dreaming for too long is never mentally health, so most will not live there, and they would need to exchange it for mundane money so they can rent apartments and buy food and so on on the mundane world.<br /> <br /> And in cities that the lords save up all dream stuff, there will probably be illegal markets, with Pookas seeling Chimerical Iron in dark alleyways at night to desperate Nockers. Besides most kiths except Nockers, Redcaps and (some) boggans being probably okay with the lord doing that, this might be the ground for a revolution or a rebellion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T22:00:45-07:00","id":1141660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141300-my-homebrew-setting-for-dream-stuff?p=1141374#post1141374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a very good setting to be honest. But if you have a economy over dreamstuff it is necessary a demand for it too. Those outposts probably have deals with market freeholds nearby to commercialize this stuff. Even far away Market Freeholds might be interested, so caravans might be taking those goods from one place to another, maybe across countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thoughts. That can really flesh out how and why different and even competing Changeling and Chimera governments interact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141300-my-homebrew-setting-for-dream-stuff?p=1141374#post1141374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, remember that staying in the Dreaming for too long is never mentally health, so most will not live there, and they would need to exchange it for mundane money so they can rent apartments and buy food and so on on the mundane world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I know. It's just in Dreams and Nighmares there was a village of Changelings in the Dreaming and I thought this might be a good retcon for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141300-my-homebrew-setting-for-dream-stuff?p=1141374#post1141374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in cities that the lords save up all dream stuff, there will probably be illegal markets, with Pookas seeling Chimerical Iron in dark alleyways at night to desperate Nockers. Besides most kiths except Nockers, Redcaps and (some) boggans being probably okay with the lord doing that, this might be the ground for a revolution or a rebellion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also good ideas. I am trying to think of the more interesting aspects of how an organized Fae civilization spread across the globe might function and how it would look like. Fae who can gather Dreamstuff with any regularity are probably as valued as the people who build trods between two points. And they probably have to be as skilled, knowledgeable of the world, and as well armed as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:40:49-07:00","id":1141764,"title":"","content":"'Glamour speakeasies'! Dross-running gangsters! Corrupt nobles getting a slice of the action!<br /> ....sounds like the 1920s. Take that imagery, and run wild with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}